# The design plan's worked example (A B C A D A on 3 lines), grown by one block to fit
# the default 4-way cache: A B C D A E A. Blocks 16 bytes apart share a set, so every
# block here lands in set 0.
#
# Run with the defaults (--cache 64 --block 4 --ways 4).
# Result: FIFO 1 hit (evicts A, then B); LRU 2 hits (evicts only B).
R 0x0000   # A
R 0x0010   # B
R 0x0020   # C
R 0x0030   # D
R 0x0000   # A: a hit for both, and LRU refreshes it
R 0x0040   # E: set 0 is full. FIFO evicts A (loaded first), LRU evicts B (used least recently)
R 0x0000   # A: FIFO misses, LRU hits
